From 314f7a7be57e0cf9cdcb743a78a983043ac5407c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:34:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] glm cuda: a decode window's shared expert on a side
 stream beside the routed experts

The MoE block ran the shared expert after the routed experts on one stream. A decode
window (not a prompt chunk) now forks the shared expert's gate/up, SwiGLU, down and
put_slot onto a second stream right after the block's input is ready, and the fill joins
it before the slot combine. The kernels, their inputs and the combine's order are
unchanged, so the bits are the same; only the overlap changes. Engine.side holds the
stream and events, made at init; TF_GLM_SHARED_SIDE=0 keeps one stream.

Measured on an RTX PRO 6000 (sm_120, bench_overlap): 70.6 -> 60.6 us a MoE layer at one
row, 96.5 -> 84.9 us at two.

